<section class="listing-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Useful, with the limits made clear</span><h1>Sources &amp; updates</h1><p class="lead">A growing editorial guide, not a claim to contain every business or every event in Antalya.</p></div></section>
<section class="discovery-section"><div class="container article-body"><h2>Hotel listings</h2><p>Our curated directory links to hotel websites and records when information was reviewed. A review date confirms a source check, not room availability, a licence audit or a guarantee that every facility operates today. We do not publish live room prices or booking inventory.</p><p>For official accommodation records, consult the <a href="https://tga.gov.tr/kultur-ve-turizm-bakanligi-belgeli-konaklama-tesisleri" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ministry-certified accommodation directory</a>.</p><h2>Events</h2><p>Confirmed dates require a source from the organiser, venue, public authority or authorised ticket seller. Undated festival guides stay separate from confirmed listings. Ended events are archived. The calendar is a reviewed snapshot, not an automatic live feed.</p><p>Check <a href="https://www.antalya.bel.tr/tr/etkinlikler" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Antalya municipality’s event calendar</a> for additional listings and always follow the linked organiser for ticket conditions, access rules, postponements and cancellations.</p><h2>What “checked” means</h2><p>Each dated check is a real editorial review, not the time the website was built. Content can become stale between reviews. A successful page request alone never counts as confirmation of an event date or hotel detail.</p><h2>Photographs and recommendations</h2><p>Regional photographs illustrate Antalya and are not evidence of a specific room or property. Hotel entries without verified property photography use text-based presentation. Itineraries and planning tips are editorial suggestions, not reservations or guaranteed schedules.</p><h2>Suggest a correction</h2><p>Send the page, the detail that needs correction and a reliable source using our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. We review information before publishing it.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/editorial-policy/">Read the editorial policy →</a></p></div></section>
